title: C3RB3r Ransomware File Encryption on Synology NAS
id: cbabeb89-d562-4a35-aba0-6db53c40a49b
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects files renamed with the .L0CK3D extension used by C3RB3r (a Cerber
    variant) during the October 2026 wave of attacks against Synology NAS
    appliances running outdated DSM. Synology confirmed the intrusion path is
    the SA-24:20 vulnerability cluster (CVE-2024-10441, CVE-2024-10445,
    CVE-2024-50629) patched in December 2024, so an encryption event here means
    the appliance was never updated and its management interface was reachable.
references:
    - https://www.synology.com/en-global/company/news/article/C3RB3R/Synology%20urges%20users%20to%20update%20DSM%20following%20ransomware%20attacks%20on%20outdated%20DSM%20versions
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/synology-warns-customers-of-ongoing-c3rb3r-ransomware-attacks/
    - https://www.synology.com/en-us/security/advisory/Synology_SA_24_20
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-11-02
tags:
    - attack.t1486
    - attack.impact
logsource:
    category: file_event
detection:
    selection_extension:
        TargetFilename|endswith: '.L0CK3D'
    selection_extension_lower:
        TargetFilename|endswith: '.l0ck3d'
    condition: selection_extension or selection_extension_lower
falsepositives:
    - User files or backup archives that legitimately carry a L0CK3D suffix (rare; verify the host is a Synology NAS with outdated DSM)
level: critical
